-- title:
--   The Cesaro Fourier transform and its remainder
-- statement:
--   Assume the Fourier identity for the tail term. For $M>0$ and an $L^2$ Cesaro approximant $g_M$, its Plancherel transform agrees almost everywhere with
--   $$\widehat J_{\mathrm{cont}}+R_M,$$
--   where $R_M$ is the explicitly defined averaged oscillatory remainder.
-- source:
--   Supporting lemma in the explicit Beurling-Selberg argument, following J. D. Vaaler, Some extremal functions in Fourier analysis, Bulletin of the AMS 12 (1985), Section 2. Original Lean source: MathExtras/NumberTheory/Analysis/VaalerCesaroFTMinorAssembly.lean, lines 59-77.

